================================================================================
GUÍA DEFINITIVA DE COMANDOS - LABORATORIO DE ALTA DISPONIBILIDAD (KEEPALIVED)
================================================================================
IP Virtual (VIP): 172.27.218.100
sudo pcs resource create IP_Flotante2 ocf:heartbeat:IPaddr2 ip=172.27.218.150 cidr_netmask=16 nic=ens160 op monitor interval=30s

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SERVIDOR MASTER (172.27.222.108)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A) Instalación y Directorios:
   sudo dnf install -y keepalived httpd --nogpgcheck
   sudo mkdir -p /etc/keepalived /var/www/holamundo

B) Configuración de Keepalived:
   Abrir archivo: sudo nano /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf
   Contenido a pegar:

global_defs {
    router_id rhel10_master
}
vrrp_script check_httpd {
    script "pidof httpd"
    interval 2
    weight 2
}
vrrp_instance VI_1 {
    state MASTER
    interface ens160
    virtual_router_id 51
    priority 101
    advert_int 1
    authentication {
        auth_type PASS
        auth_pass SecHttp123
    }
    virtual_ipaddress {
        172.27.218.100/16
    }
    track_script {
        check_httpd
    }
}

C) Configuración Web, Firewall y Servicios:
   echo "<h1>Hola desde SERVER 1 (Master - 172.27.222.108)</h1>" | sudo tee /var/www/holamundo/index.html
   sudo chmod 644 /var/www/holamundo/index.html
   sudo rm -f /etc/httpd/conf.d/welcome.conf
   sudo firewall-cmd --add-service=http --permanent
   sudo firewall-cmd --add-protocol=vrrp --permanent
   sudo firewall-cmd --reload
   sudo systemctl enable --now httpd
   sudo systemctl enable --now keepalived

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. SERVIDOR BACKUP (172.27.218.146)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A) Instalación y Directorios:
   sudo dnf install -y keepalived httpd --nogpgcheck
   sudo mkdir -p /etc/keepalived /var/www/holamundo

B) Configuración de Keepalived:
   Abrir archivo: sudo nano /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf
   Contenido a pegar:

global_defs {
    router_id rhel10_backup
}
vrrp_script check_httpd {
    script "pidof httpd"
    interval 2
    weight 2
}
vrrp_instance VI_1 {
    state BACKUP
    interface ens224
    virtual_router_id 51
    priority 100
    advert_int 1
    authentication {
        auth_type PASS
        auth_pass SecHttp123
    }
    virtual_ipaddress {
        172.27.218.100/16
    }
    track_script {
        check_httpd
    }
}

C) Configuración Web, Firewall y Servicios:
   echo "<h1>Hola desde SERVER 2 (Backup - 172.27.218.146)</h1>" | sudo tee /var/www/holamundo/index.html
   sudo chmod 644 /var/www/holamundo/index.html
   sudo firewall-cmd --add-service=http --permanent
   sudo firewall-cmd --add-protocol=vrrp --permanent
   sudo firewall-cmd --reload
   sudo systemctl enable --now httpd
   sudo systemctl enable --now keepalived

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. COMANDOS DE DIAGNÓSTICO Y PRUEBAS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Ver si la IP Virtual está levantada en la interfaz:
  ip addr show

- Probar localmente qué responde Apache:
  curl http://localhost

- Simular la caída apagando Apache en el Master:
  sudo systemctl stop httpd

- Recuperar el estado inicial encendiendo Apache en el Master:
  sudo systemctl start httpd
